\",\"pushedServices\":{},\"pendingPushedServices\":{},\"originalSize\":\"1080x1080\",\"recordTypeLabel\":\"image\"}],\"pushedServices\":{},\"pendingPushedServices\":{},\"originalSize\":\"1080x1080\",\"recordTypeLabel\":\"store-item\"},{\"id\":\"68da5957b07f5411ead70c17\",\"collectionId\":\"604e95de63949d1dc619f0de\",\"recordType\":11,\"addedOn\":1632383201443,\"updatedOn\":1788087156616,\"displayIndex\":0,\"starred\":false,\"passthrough\":false,\"tags\":[\"Subculture Screenings\",\"Faye Dunaway\"],\"categoryIds\":[\"604e95de63949d1dc619f0f4\"],\"workflowState\":1,\"publishOn\":1759140300364,\"authorId\":\"5f3bff9c2865d009ade5e427\",\"systemDataId\":\"1ef6b32d-dc15-4ba3-804e-0c96795f2cc5\",\"systemDataVariants\":\"1080x1080,100w,300w,500w,750w,1000w\",\"systemDataSourceType\":\"JPEG\",\"filename\":\"2.jpg\",\"mediaFocalPoint\":{\"x\":0.5,\"y\":0.5,\"source\":3},\"colorData\":{\"topLeftAverage\":\"414141\",\"topRightAverage\":\"414141\",\"bottomLeftAverage\":\"3c3125\",\"bottomRightAverage\":\"343434\",\"centerAverage\":\"878787\",\"suggestedBgColor\":\"525150\"},\"urlId\":\"droog-7w73f-hg8bp-y7rkt-3gjsk-f6pe8-352bw-3nstx-g5pwl-5gk3k-wbbrf-zfdft-m3sgj-bzw8t-p574z-cx7wt-sl3pk-ryyya-s5rd4\",\"title\":\"WITHNAIL AND I - Tues 14 Oct 2025 7pm - All is Joy Soho\",\"body\":null,\"excerpt\":\"<p style=\\\"white-space:pre-wrap;\\\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\\\"true\\\">As part of Cine Style the iconic Withnail and I at All is Joy </p><p style=\\\"white-space:pre-wrap;\\\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\\\"true\\\">London. The 1960s. Two unemployed actors\\u2014acerbic, elegantly wasted (and oh so stylish \\u2026)</p><p style=\\\"white-space:pre-wrap;\\\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\\\"true\\\"><span>Danny: \\u201CHas he just been busted?\\u201D </span><br />Marwood: \\u201CNo.\\u201D <br />Danny: \\u201CThen why's he wearing that old suit?\\u201D<br />Withnail: \\u201COld suit! This suit was cut by Hawke's of Savile Row.&nbsp;Just because the best tailoring you've ever seen is above your fucking appendix doesn't mean anything.\\u201C</p><p style=\\\"white-space:pre-wrap;\\\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\\\"true\\\">Withnail (Richard E. Grant) and the anxiety-ridden &quot;I&quot; (Paul McGann)\\u2014drown their frustrations in booze, pills, and lighter fluid.</p><p style=\\\"white-space:pre-wrap;\\\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\\\"true\\\">From designer Andrea Galer\\u2019s iconic coat (Andrea was the wardrobe assistant on Hail The New Puritan which we showed at All is Joy earlier this year) to Marwood\\u2019s boiled wool jumper, leather coat and matinee idol fedora the costumes are as piss elegant (in an aristocratically moth eaten way) as Withnail and Marwood are pissed \\u2026</p><p style=\\\"white-space:pre-wrap;\\\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\\\"true\\\">When Withnail's Uncle Monty (Richard Griffiths) offers his cottage, they escape the squalor of their flat for a week in the country. They soon realize they\\u2019ve gone on holiday by mistake when their wits\\u2014and friendship\\u2014are sorely tested by violent downpours, less than hospitable locals, and empty cupboards. An intelligent, superbly acted, and hilarious film, Bruce Robinson\\u2019s semi-autobiographical cult favourite is laugh out loud funny\\u2026</p><p style=\\\"white-space:pre-wrap;\\\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\\\"true\\\">7pm: DOORS - DJ</p><p style=\\\"white-space:pre-wrap;\\\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\\\"true\\\">7.30pm: Introduction with Chris McGill (Rebel Reel Cine Club)</p><p style=\\\"white-space:pre-wrap;\\\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\\\"true\\\">8pm: Withnail and I</p><p style=\\\"white-space:pre-wrap;\\\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\\\"true\\\">DJ until Midnight</p><p style=\\\"white-space:pre-wrap;\\\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\\\"true\\\"><strong>Withnail and I</strong><br />Dir. Bruce Robinson 1987<br />1hr 47 mins</p><p style=\\\"white-space:pre-wrap;\\\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\\\"true\\\">Buy a Cine Style 2025 pass for 2 or more films.</p><p style=\\\"white-space:pre-wrap;\\\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\\\"true\\\">Save when you buy - this allows you to come to any of the films - please message us to confirm which films you\\u2019d like to come to.</p><p style=\\\"white-space:pre-wrap;\\\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\\\"true\\\">CINE STYLE 2025</p><p style=\\\"white-space:pre-wrap;\\\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\\\"true\\\">Presented by Rebel Reel Cine Club with Vadim Kosmos&nbsp;</p><p style=\\\"white-space:pre-wrap;\\\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\\\"true\\\"><strong>The Old Ivy House, <span>166 Goswell Rd, London EC1V 7DT</span></strong></p><p style=\\\"white-space:pre-wrap;\\\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\\\"true\\\">Monday 13th October 7pm<br /><strong>Saturday Night Fever</strong> Dir. John Badham 1977 1hr 59mins<br />DJ Vadim Kosmos<br /><br /><strong>All Is Joy Soho, &nbsp;75 Dean St, London W1D 3PU&nbsp;</strong></p><p style=\\\"white-space:pre-wrap;\\\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\\\"true\\\"><strong>Tuesday 14 October 7pm<br />Withnail and I</strong> Dir. Bruce Robinson 1987 1hr 47 mins<br />DJ Martin Green and Vadim Kosmos</p><p style=\\\"white-space:pre-wrap;\\\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\\\"true\\\"><strong>Wednesday 15 October 7pm<br /><span>The Eyes of Laura Mars</span></strong> Dir. Irving Kershner 1978 1hr 44 mins<strong><span><br />DJ Sonia Shadid (Hot Pants Nights)</span></strong></p><p style=\\\"white-space:pre-wrap;\\\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\\\"true\\\">Friday 17 October 7pm <br /><strong><span>Querelle </span></strong>Dir. Rainer Fassbender 1982 1hr 47 mins<br />DJ before and after</p><p style=\\\"white-space:pre-wrap;\\\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\\\"true\\\">Sunday 19 October 4pm<br /><strong><span>Fallen Angels</span></strong> Dir. Wong Kar Wei 1995 1hr 33 mins<br />Before and after</p>\",\"likeCount\":0,\"commentCount\":0,\"publicCommentCount\":0,\"commentState\":1,\"unsaved\":false,\"fullUrl\":\"/bookhere/p/droog-7w73f-hg8bp-y7rkt-3gjsk-f6pe8-352bw-3nstx-g5pwl-5gk3k-wbbrf-zfdft-m3sgj-bzw8t-p574z-cx7wt-sl3pk-ryyya-s5rd4\